driveLeakT -- F-125, A DRIVE'S MESSAGE MUST NOT LEAVE ITS INDENTATION OR AN OPEN define IN THE CALLER (2026-09-24).
fxE drives ExpressioN over an indented message ("define", then "  aa isRule;"), which leaves lastIndent at 2. fxS drives
StatemenT over "define aa isRule; ;", which stops before the closing ; and leaves defining at 1 (processFlags case D
toggles it). Either alone, the caller continues; both, and the caller's next statement fails to match and the rest of
this file is ABANDONED at exit 0. driveStep (and jitProbeDrive, which copies its lines) now restore the caller's
lastIndent and defining at the pop, as they already restored inputFloor.

pop.sh asserts EXACT lines: DL RETURNED and the sentinel. H7, measured at landing: with neither restore, both lines
are missing; with EITHER restore alone they print -- so both leaks were real and each was sufficient here.
